        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "FeCl2·4H2O (1.0 mmol, 0.199 g) was dissolved in CH3CN/CH2Cl2 (10 mL:10 mL) and mixed with a solution of N-methyldiethanolamine (1.0 mmol, 0.119 g) in 5.0 mL CH3CN, Nd(NO3)3·6H2O (1.0 mmol, 0.438 g), CH3COONa (1.0 mmol, 0.082 g), and dropwise triethylamine. The mixture was stirred for 2 h, filtered, and washed with CH3CN. The filtrate was left undisturbed at room temperature for slow evaporation; reddish crystals appeared within a week and were dried in open air.",
